<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<fdmmaterial version="1.3" xmlns="http://www.ultimaker.com/material" xmlns:cura="http://www.ultimaker.com/cura">
  <metadata>
    <name>
      <brand>Clay</brand>
      <material>Clay</material>
      <color>Generic</color>
      <label>Clay</label>
    </name>
    <description>Clay is a stiff, sticky fine-grained earth, typically yellow, red, or bluish-gray in color and often forming an impermeable layer in the soil. It can be molded when wet, and is dried and baked to make bricks, pottery, and ceramics.</description>
    <adhesion_info>Printing on top of a clay slab has the best results. You can also print on a damp surface and print the base, but you may need to adjust 1st layer width and the extrusion rate. When a print starts you should increase the extrusion rate momentarily to get a good flow rate started, and then bring the extrusion back to normal rates once clay is comeing out.</adhesion_info>
    <GUID>7c60cb43-4ec7-437d-a5fe-7b5723243075</GUID>
    <version>7</version>
    <color_code>#55aaff</color_code>
  </metadata>
